1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:18,411
This video is for the platform team, the super admins who look after every
organization on NTSOne. You will see accounts, the inbox, payments, the platform fund,
maintenance, backups and the audit log. The data shown is demonstration data.

2
00:00:19,011 --> 00:00:32,494
A super admin has extra items in the menu: Accounts, Inbox, Payments, Platform fund,
Backup and Recovery, Maintenance and Audit log. These are only visible to the platform
team.

3
00:00:33,094 --> 00:00:56,794
Accounts lists every organization, its owner, and how many users, programs, polls and
businesses it has. Open one to see its users, which you can suspend or reactivate, and
its programs. Here you also set that organization's payment terms: the platform fee,
the waiting time before money can be withdrawn, and when withdrawals switch on.

4
00:00:57,394 --> 00:01:12,876
The inbox gathers everything people send to the platform team: feedback from inside
the app, messages from the contact form, and reports of concerns. Open a message to
read it, reply by email, and mark it resolved.

5
00:01:13,476 --> 00:01:32,747
The Payments page shows what every organization has been paid, the fees taken,
refunds, withdrawals and what is left in each fund. Below, you approve or decline
large withdrawals and refunds, and look at payments that need a check. A request can't
be approved by the person who made it.

6
00:01:33,347 --> 00:01:51,439
The platform fund is the platform's own money: the fees it keeps from every payment.
You can see the balance, add a withdrawal account, withdraw, and follow every fee in
Money in and out. In this demo, Monime is not connected, so withdrawing is switched
off.

7
00:01:52,039 --> 00:02:13,450
When you need to work on the system, turn on Maintenance mode. Write the message
people will see, give an expected time back, and choose to show a message at the top
of the page or replace the page. You can show it everywhere or only on some parts, and
email team members and voters once. The platform team is never locked out.

8
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:33,721
A full, encrypted copy of the database is made every day and checked before it counts.
You can back up now, verify a backup, download it, or restore from it, and every
restore is recorded with a safety copy taken first. The retention settings decide how
long old backups are kept.

9
00:02:34,321 --> 00:02:51,473
The audit log records every action in the system, grouped by account: who did it, what
they did, when, and whether it worked. Search it, filter by date, result or person,
and export it. Records cannot be changed or removed.

10
00:02:52,073 --> 00:02:58,546
That is how the platform team looks after NTSOne. Use this video as your guide.
